The `Markdown` component from `react-markdown` can accept custom component definitions to use when rendering markdown content:

https://github.com/OpenDevin/OpenDevin/blob/733bf2b38cd7d29f5d87c1cef49d342298217bb3/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatMessage.tsx#L80-L82

In the case of an `ol`, Tailwind CSS resets the styles which could be reverted (something like this):

```css
.markdown > ol {
  all: revert;
}
```

To apply custom styles like margin, you can pass a custom component:

```tsx
<Markdown
  components={{
    code,
    ul: ({ children }) => <ul className="list-disc ml-5">{children}</ul>,
  }}
>
  {message.content}
</Markdown>
```

You can read more [here](https://github.com/remarkjs/react-markdown?tab=readme-ov-file#appendix-b-components)

